.TH PLUGIN\-HOSTD 1 "September 2026" "plugin-hostd 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin\-hostd \- supervisor of plugin host processes behind one mod\-host protocol socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin\-hostd
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR file ]
.br
.B plugin\-hostd
.RB [ \-V | \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B plugin\-hostd
speaks mod\-host's socket protocol to a controller and runs one worker process per plugin, or per named
pool of plugins, behind it: a plugin that crashes takes down its own worker and nothing else, and the
daemon puts it back. Workers are
.BR mod\-host (1)
for LV2 plugins and
.BR omx\-clap\-host (1)
for CLAP plugins, each started as
.B \-n \-p
.IR port .
Audio never passes through the daemon: every worker is a jack client named
.BI effect_ instance
as in mod\-host, and links are made in the graph.
.PP
It prints
.B plugin\-hostd ready!
once both ports accept. No worker exists until the first
.BR add .
.B quit
or SIGTERM stops every worker and the daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-socket\-port =\fIport\fR
Command port (default 5555).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-feedback\-port =\fIport\fR
Feedback port (default the command port plus one, unless
.B \-n
is given).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config =\fIfile\fR
Settings file.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nofork
Accepted; the daemon never forks.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help text and exit.
.SH FILES
The settings live in
.IR file ,
in
.B $PLUGIN_HOSTD_CONF
or in
.IR ~/.config/plugin\-hostd.conf ,
one
.RI \(dq key " value" \(dq
per line: mod_host, clap_host (the worker programs), lv2_path, state_root, ready_timeout_ms,
rpc_timeout_ms, backoff_base_ms, backoff_max_ms, storm_deaths, storm_window_ms, suspect_window_ms, checkpoint_ms and pool_max.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mod\-host (1),
.BR omx\-clap\-host (1)
.PP
The protocol, the placement of an instance, the verbs the daemon adds and the events on the feedback port are
described in the README of the source tree.
